DESCRIPTION<<VER_END
PRE 4.2.0 (#302, #303 on cursor/p3-issues-279-302-303):

#302 — post-PR #301 cleanup
- contract_p3_wire.h: fl_net_endpoint_t at contract layer (wire rev 4); fl_net_server_addr_t typedef alias; drop net_endpoint.c layout _Static_asserts
- server_shared_db: catalog message transfer_id is UUID v4 (OpenSSL RAND_bytes) with PRIMARY KEY retry (up to 3 attempts)
- FL_CONTRACT_P3_NETWORKING_REV 17

#303 — IPv6 UI/UX (foundation from #280 / PR #301)
- fl_net_endpoint_format: a.b.c.d:port or [addr]:port
- fl_net_route_snapshot6; ifconfig prints inet / inet6 from route tables (loopback inet6 ::1 prefixlen 128)
- Shell: ping6; nslookup and resolve print A + AAAA; server host/join/connected use formatted endpoints
- fl_net_endpoint_parse_bind: server join -bind accepts bare IPv4/IPv6 (port 0) for multi-IP demos
- OP_MEMBER_LIST_SNAPSHOT optional peer tail (family/port/addr); client roster shows [addr]:port
- ping6 batch tokenizer matches ping (-c/-W then host)
- fl_net_icmpv6_echo_exchange and fl_net_ping6 for loopback ICMPv6

#279 — Wi-Fi 802.11ax foundation (P3-10)
- contract_p3_wifi.h promoted; FL_CONTRACT_P3_NETWORKING_REV 18; net_wifi_he IE parser
- SQLite wifi_router table (name, hashed password, salt, BSSID/band/channel/auth/HE makeup, join state) in userland/shell/fl_wifi.db
- Shell: wifi scan, wifi join <name> [password], wifi known; hosted lab scan/join until P4 NIC
- Docs: P3-10 module ~✅ in ROADMAP/P3_NETWORKING; docs/GITHUB_ISSUE_SYNC_279.md for #279 checklist
VER_END

RELEASE_DATE=2026-06-02
